[Puzzle "The long diagonal"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "6.Qf3"]
[End "6.Qf3"]
[Hint "Black's pawns have left the long diagonal from f3 to a8. What stands at the end of it?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e3 b5 4. a4 c6 5. axb5 cxb5? 6. Qf3! {[%cal Gf3a8] Hits the rook on a8, which can't move. Black can block with a piece, but then loses that piece.}
(6. b3? {Hits the chain, but it is much slower.} 6... Bb7 7. bxc4 bxc4 8. Bxc4 e6 {White has the pawn back, but no more. Stockfish: +0.4, slightly better for White.})
6... Nc6 7. Qxc6+ Bd7 8. Qa6 {White is a piece up, and the b5 pawn is next. Stockfish: +5.5, winning for White.}
*

[Puzzle "The pinned knight on c3"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Win material"]
[Solve "8...Nxc3"]
[End "9...Bxc3+"]
[Hint "White's knight on c3 is pinned to the king. How many times can you take it?"]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. Nc3 e5 4. d5 Nf6 5. e4 b5 6. Nxb5 Nxe4 7. Bxc4 Bb4+ 8. Nc3?? Nxc3! {[%cal Gc3d1] Takes the pinned knight and hits the queen.}
9. bxc3 Bxc3+! {[%hint The bishop can take back with check. What else does it hit?] [%cal Gc3a1] Check, and the bishop hits the rook on a1.}
10. Bd2 Bxa1 11. Qxa1 {Black has won a rook and a pawn for a bishop. Stockfish: −3.7, winning for Black.}
*

[Puzzle "Mate in two"]
[Type "puzzle"]
[Theme "Checkmate in 2"]
[Solve "7.Bxf7+"]
[End "8.Qe6#"]
[Hint "Black has just taken your knight. Look at f7 and e6."]

1. d4 d5 2. c4 dxc4 3. e3 Nf6 4. Bxc4 Nc6 5. Nf3 Bg4 6. Qb3 Bxf3?? 7. Bxf7+! {[%cal Gc4f7] Check. The queen on b3 guards the bishop, so the king can't take it.}
(7. gxf3? {Takes the bishop back, but misses mate.} 7... e6 8. Qxb7 Nb4 9. Bb5+ Nd7 {White is a pawn up. Stockfish: +1.7, clearly better for White.})
7... Kd7 8. Qe6# {[%hint The king has gone to d7. Find the queen move it can't escape.] Checkmate.}
*
